-- Live tickets (Oct–Nov 2026) --------------------------------------------------
-- What a demo user sees as current on 2026-11-20 (Fri). Every ticket follows the
-- D39–D43 flow: create → triage (classify, contractor flag, `triaged` marker, next
-- step) → statuses/schedule dates. The tickets row is the fold of its events.
--   Ball with the agent (open):   205 untriaged and breached (the concierge's comment
--                                 doesn't acknowledge, D40); 212 untriaged, still on time;
--                                 8 resident replied, handed back (D39); 5 board approved.
--   Waiting on others (paused):   7 awaiting the resident ~8 days; 2 awaiting the Board
--                                 for a lift quote; 1 auto-closed after 14 days (D39).
--   Pending 3rd party:            3 future schedule date; 9 date is today; 206 date was
--                                 yesterday and SecureEntry attended; 209 contractor flagged
--                                 after triage; 204 attended, parts on order.
--   Closed as duplicate (D42):    207 and 210 of 206; 208 of 3.
--   Resolved: 4 (cleaning), 6 (after a hand-back), 211 (at triage), 203 (breaches Enquiry to contractor and Cleaning resolved), 200.
-- Contractor email demo (UJ-04), D21/D24/D43:
--   200 GreenScape  — domain registered: reply classified contractor, all clocks met.
--   201 AquaHeat    — contractor asks to confirm a slot, agent goes quiet:
--                     'Reply to contractor', 'Chase silent contractor' and
--                     '3rd-party follow-up' all breached.
--   202 Fixit       — operative replies from gmail: unknown sender, no role (D43), queued
--                     in Unknown senders, so the contractor looks silent. Link the sender
--                     to Fixit to re-score.
--   203 WindowShine — domain not registered: the agent's enquiry isn't recognised
--                     (no `enquiry_sent` marker, so 'Enquiry to contractor' breaches), the
--                     reply is from an unknown sender with no role (D43).
--   204 Hugo's damp patch: the agent emails asking for a photo (triage, awaiting_resident);
--       Hugo's email reply with the photo hands it back (D39, D28). R2 objects live in
--       server/dev-seed-files/; `npm run seed:dev` uploads them.

